          "final_text_tail": "ained groups with `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_ctx:`\n     - Wrapped sub-context creation for chained groups with `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_sub_ctx:`\n   - Ensures all file handles and resources managed by contexts are closed when going out of scope during shell completion, eliminating `ResourceWarning` leaks.\n\n2. **Task 2: Add `cleanup_timeout` parameter to `Context` to prevent hanging close operations**\n   - In [`src/click/core.py`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-cxn9okg6/repo/src/click/core.py):\n     - Added `cleanup_timeout: float | None = None` parameter to [`Context.__init__`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-cxn9okg6/repo/src/click/core.py#L270-L287).\n     - Validated `cleanup_timeout`: must be a positive float (> 0) when specified; raises `ValueError` if zero, negative, or not a positive float; inherits from `parent` if not provided.\n     - Updated [`Context.close`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-cxn9okg6/repo/src/click/core.py#L622): when `cleanup_timeout` is set, wraps cleanup operations with a daemon worker thread joined with a timeout. If the timeout is exceeded, logs a warning message and terminates wait gracefully; re-raises any exception raised during cleanup if completed within timeout.\n   - Shell completion contexts naturally respect `cleanup_timeout` through `Context` initialization and context manager exit.\n",
